- [P1] [context-clarity.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb/scripts/repo-prune/bin/context-clarity.sh:196): the metric is still hardcoded to seven §3 items. The comments at [lines 103-106](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb/scripts/repo-prune/bin/context-clarity.sh:103) claim growth in §3 will show up automatically, but the loop is literally `for _i in 1 2 3 4 5 6 7`. Add a new `8.` item to §3 and the metric neither changes nor fails. That is exactly the silent under-report the design says it prevents. Status: Reasoned.

- [P1] [context-clarity.sh](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb/scripts/repo-prune/bin/context-clarity.sh:161): the extractor drops any backticked token that does not end with literal `.md`. A materially changed §3 item that adds `` `foo` ``, `` `foo.txt` ``, or even `` `foo.md#section` `` to an otherwise resolving item is invisible: the guard stays green and the count stays flat. That breaks the claimed “add a file -> count +1” control for plausible Markdown edits. Status: Reasoned.

- [P2] [steward-cold-start-budget.md](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb/dev/design/steward-cold-start-budget.md:93) and [steward-cold-start-budget.md](/home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb/dev/design/steward-cold-start-budget.md:189): the proposal contradicts itself on the gating artifact. Phase 0 explicitly says not to add a parallel `steward-coldstart-cost.sh`; Phase 4 later says to wire `steward-coldstart-cost.sh` into CI. Concrete failure scenario: an implementer following Phase 4 recreates the redundant script that Phase 0 just rejected, or stalls on which artifact actually owns the ceiling gate. Status: Confirmed by reading.

